cue0020573
01:05:35.024 --> 01:05:41.024
And therefore, it is not the halakha like that. You see, that's the notion of Nasiblah,

cue0020574
01:05:41.024 --> 01:05:47.024
Al-Ibbaletanae. Al-Ibbaletanae is exactly the opposite of what Rashi says.

cue0020575
01:05:47.024 --> 01:05:56.184
Now that he believes in it, Naseeblah, not Aliba de Dede, is exactly the opposite of what Rashi said.

cue0020576
01:05:56.184 --> 01:05:59.024
You know, look what Rashi says.

cue0020577
01:05:59.024 --> 01:06:05.824
Rashi says, Naseebleh, Aliba, Tanae, Ben Rubem, Galeem, Sava, Lakera, Banan,

cue0020578
01:06:05.824 --> 01:06:09.564
or Kohesh, Yahava, Sava, no, no, Izzat, I am not suffering like that.

cue0020579
01:06:09.564 --> 01:06:14.764
Naseeblah, Aliba, why do you say that? Aliba is Tanae, Tanae means, Makhloket Tanaim.

cue0020580
01:06:14.764 --> 01:06:22.364
And therefore, now comes the power of Hanam, Rav Yohanan, we have it in Masechet Yom HaHalakha Ke Rav Yoseph.

cue0020581
01:06:22.364 --> 01:06:30.364
Why? Because this Mishna is not a Seta Mishna. It's not a Mishna that Satam ota Rabbi Meir, Rabbeinu Qadosh.

cue0020582
01:06:30.364 --> 01:06:36.064
It's a Mishna that Naseebla, he's reciting as he received it, he received it in this Nashon.

cue0020583
01:06:36.064 --> 01:06:42.264
Naseebla means I recited by a rat. And Naseebla means I recited the way somebody told me.

cue0020584
01:06:42.264 --> 01:06:51.704
I'm not making a Pesaḥ, that's not my Pesaḥ, it's only a recitation. I'm transmitting to you here a text. I'm not making here a Pesaḥ.

cue0020585
01:06:51.704 --> 01:07:03.464
Alright? So therefore, Nasiv Lach, Rabbi Alephadet Annaeh, the opposite exactly of what Rashi says, and that is the way Rambam makes a Pesaḥ Halakha,

cue0020586
