cue0020595
01:08:25.036 --> 01:08:28.036
Sugyah 22.

cue0020596
01:08:28.036 --> 01:08:35.036
And Ben Bamah Gedolah Rehomah Ketanah Elah Pesaḥim.

cue0020597
01:08:35.036 --> 01:09:02.036
Now, prior to the erection of the temple, there were, there was no Bet hammiqdash, and therefore there were Bamod. Bamod means altars. Altars means it's not a fixed place, it's a kind of a temporary situation, and so that's what it was.

cue0020598
01:09:02.036 --> 01:09:09.036
So there were two types of Bama. Bama Gedolah, which belongs to the Sepur.

cue0020599
01:09:09.036 --> 01:09:25.036
And then there is Bama Ketanah, which is a private Bama, something that an individual does it for himself.

cue0020600
01:09:25.036 --> 01:09:37.036
So now, the Bamar Gedolah was, for instance, in Nob, in Shiloh, they were Bamot, yes? It was the part of the Mishkan, you know, the ancient Mishkan.

cue0020601
01:09:37.036 --> 01:09:45.036
It means, by virtue of being the Mishkan, means that it's temporary. Still, we did not arrive to the Petah Migdash.

cue0020602
01:09:45.036 --> 01:09:53.036
And it has a Bamar Gedolah, and then there's a Bamar Gash. So what's the difference? The difference is only one.

cue0020603
01:09:53.036 --> 01:09:55.036
She'elna Pesaḥim.

cue0020604
01:09:55.036 --> 01:09:57.756
That Pesaḥim is an interesting Qorban.

cue0020605
01:09:57.756 --> 01:10:00.056
And it has to be, and let me explain to you.

cue0020606
01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:12.200
Of course, the two types of korbanot. There is Qorban yachid. Yachid means Aula, Bahatat, Asham, Shalamin.

cue0020607
01:10:12.200 --> 01:10:17.400
So there is Qorban yachid. Then there is Qorban sabbur.

cue0020608
01:10:17.400 --> 01:10:26.600
That the only the obligation, the incumbent is the community at large.

cue0020609
01:10:26.600 --> 01:10:34.600
For instance, Tamikshat Shachar, Tamikshat Awaim, Musafim, all the Musafim. So this is Qorban Sebur.

cue0020610
01:10:34.600 --> 01:10:40.600
Now, I have a whole theory about Qorban Pesaḥ, but Qorban Pesaḥ is the only exception.

cue0020611
01:10:40.600 --> 01:10:47.600
But on the one hand, there is a particular obligation on the individual to bring Qorban Pesaḥ.

cue0020612
01:10:47.600 --> 01:10:54.600
And therefore, from this point of view, it's not a Qorban Sebur, it's Qorban Yahid.

cue0020613
01:10:54.600 --> 01:11:03.900
For instance, I don't have to bring a Koran Tami, Shekh Shachar, Shekhar Avaim. I'm not a Sabur, I'm just a Yahid.

cue0020614
01:11:03.900 --> 01:11:09.900
On the other hand, the Yahid has the obligation to bring, just like you have to bring a Chattat.

cue0020615
01:11:09.900 --> 01:11:15.500
You have to bring a Koran Pesaḥ. It's more than a Chattat. A Chattat doesn't have a fixed date.

cue0020616
01:11:15.500 --> 01:11:19.700
Here you have a fixed date. Koran Pesaḥ, you have to bring it.

cue0020617
01:11:19.700 --> 01:11:39.700
On the other hand, it has in many aspects, has the status of Qorban Sabur. For instance, Tum'a Ni'thit, Tum'at Wa Rabim, Tera'a wa Sabur, Tema'im, as we have in the Tora, then you could bring Qorban Pesaḥ with Tum'a.

cue0020618
01:11:39.700 --> 01:11:47.460
Like if it is a Qorban sabur. It has other aspects of Qorban sabur also.

cue0020619
01:11:47.460 --> 01:11:55.220
So what is exactly Qorban Pesaḥ? I'm not entering into the particulars of this Qorban and the whole subject of Qorban.

cue0020620
01:11:55.220 --> 01:12:01.380
I hope the Ulam gives me the opportunity in life and intelligence to understand the Kadashim.

cue0020621
01:12:01.380 --> 01:12:07.060
But the point about the Qorban Pesaḥ is that it is a special kind of sabur.

cue0020622
01:12:07.060 --> 01:12:11.440
So it says, the only thing is that the only difference is Qorban Pesaḥim.

cue0020623
01:12:11.440 --> 01:12:13.940
Pesaḥim, what's the point?

cue0020624
01:12:13.940 --> 01:12:17.700
That Pesaḥim, you only could bring it in Bama Kedola.

cue0020625
01:12:17.700 --> 01:12:21.100
Because here again, it represents a kind of a sabur,

cue0020626
01:12:21.100 --> 01:12:37.394
whereas you know but you cannot be in Ketana in Bama Ketana So therefore again let me repeat So En B Kitana Ela Qorban Pesaḥim Belvad In other words like Qorban Pesaḥim you cannot bring it in Bama Kitana

cue0020627
01:12:37.394 --> 01:12:40.754
All the other things you could bring in Bama Kitana.

cue0020628
01:12:40.754 --> 01:12:44.834
And of course, the Gemaraʾ later on is going to try to analyze this point.

cue0020629
01:12:44.834 --> 01:12:50.354
Alright? So now, so now this is the Gemaraʾ.

cue0020630
01:12:50.354 --> 01:12:53.354
So that's the thing.

cue0020631
01:12:53.354 --> 01:12:58.354
Koshe hu nedar v'nedar kare b'mamah.

cue0020632
01:12:58.354 --> 01:13:00.354
It means b'mamah, b'mamah kitanna. You know how it is.

cue0020633
01:13:00.354 --> 01:13:02.354
If you could make a nedabah out of it,

cue0020634
01:13:02.354 --> 01:13:05.354
for instance, the Pesaḥ would say that he is mitnadev ola.

cue0020635
01:13:05.354 --> 01:13:08.354
He is mitnadev shelamin. Yes?

cue0020636
01:13:08.354 --> 01:13:12.354
Or torav, which is a part of another kind of shelamin.

cue0020637
01:13:12.354 --> 01:13:14.354
That you could bring in b'mamah kitanna.

cue0020638
01:13:14.354 --> 01:13:17.354
Now, there's a command that you cannot be mitnadev.

cue0020639
01:13:17.354 --> 01:13:24.854
You cannot say I'm going to bring a Nedabah and I'm going to bring a Echatat. Echatat no, it's not said you're Hayav, you're not Hayav.

cue0020640
01:13:24.854 --> 01:13:37.854
The same thing is with Pesaḥim, you can say that the person said that you're Mitnadev to give Pesaḥim, because Pesaḥim is the 14th, or you're Hayav, you're not Hayav, you're Arel, you're not Arel, you're Tameh, whatever it is.

cue0020641
01:13:37.854 --> 01:13:46.854
So this one is a korbanot, that you're not Mitnadev. So if im eno Mitnadev, so then you cannot bring it im vama ketana.

cue0020642
01:13:46.854 --> 01:14:07.334
So, I mean, incidentally, you understand why you don't have to, you cannot bring Qorban Pesaḥ to Mimavakitana because Eino Mitnate, all those things are, they have to be studied within the whole context of Korbanot, which is Korbanot means to the Qalashim Abraham, etc.

cue0020643
01:14:07.334 --> 01:14:19.334
And Seder Taharot are the most difficult sedarim that we have. And they have not been since Rambam was the first and last person who examined those sedarim thoroughly.

cue0020644
01:14:19.334 --> 01:14:25.334
And of course they have to, they need to be reexamined and studied again. But anyhow, so now this is the Qiral.

cue0020645
01:14:25.334 --> 01:14:40.334
And you see, kol she'enu lo neddav, neddav is between neddava and neddav, neddava is on the object, I'm going to bring that sheep as, she'lami, whatever it is, or neddav means I am is on the person.

cue0020646
01:14:40.334 --> 01:14:44.854
Eno Karev, Bebama, Ketana.

cue0020647
01:14:44.854 --> 01:14:47.854
Koshe, Eno, Lo Neddar.

cue0020648
01:14:47.854 --> 01:14:51.894
Lo Neddar, Eno Karev, Bebama, Ketana.

