01:15:08.988 --> 01:15:12.988
So, that comes to Gemaraʾ, it makes the following diuk.

cue0020652
01:15:12.988 --> 01:15:16.988
Tesachim, the only difference is in Tesachim.

cue0020653
01:15:16.988 --> 01:15:18.988
Tesachim you cannot bring.

cue0020654
01:15:18.988 --> 01:15:20.988
What about Amitabh i Chosaha?

cue0020655
01:15:20.988 --> 01:15:38.648
I bring it there, yes. Betula. There's no other way. I bring, I don't know, Hashem Sabur, Hashem, you know, could I bring, for instance, if they, if a robber Sabur made a Avon of Allah's Zara, could I bring this Koran?

cue0020656
01:15:38.648 --> 01:15:49.528
He says, no. He says, Besahe Betula. Emak Ke'en Besahe. And this Rashi is very good. Let me read for you Rashi Yambot.

cue0020657
01:15:49.528 --> 01:15:55.048
Pesaḥim betula, yakatane sefah, ko sheenu nidav v'nidav, eno karim v'ma'akit anna.

cue0020658
01:15:55.048 --> 01:15:58.048
And so therefore, in Israel, I cannot bring even a hatat.

cue0020659
01:15:58.048 --> 01:15:59.328
A private hatat I cannot bring.

cue0020660
01:15:59.328 --> 01:16:03.648
If I meet a rabbon and I need to bring a hatat, I cannot bring it over ma'akit anna.

cue0020661
01:16:03.648 --> 01:16:09.488
Bilo begit ʿolam. Hayim akribim, korvarot tzipur, temlimu, musafim, l'kasar kab'atim.

cue0020662
